generated_hash =

// @vibe/compiler/normalize — the `vibe normalize` canonicalizing source
// transform (parse -> module flatten -> DCE -> categorize -> re-render), plus
// the two RC-enabling pure AST rewrites codegen runs before building each
// function's Perceus plan: lift_match_scrutinees (#703/#708) and
// uniquify_shadowed_bindings (#712/#715). First COMPILER-INTERNAL contract
// batch (ADR-0070 Phase 3, #897) — unlike the stdlib batches, this package
// is compiled into the compiler itself via compiler_sources_manifest.tsv
// (group `normalize`, dual-row: this contract + normalize.vibe).
//
// The old index.vibe was not a facade but the whole implementation (the
// package is single-file), so it moved verbatim to normalize.vibe and this
// contract declares its four exported fns. No exported types, no `version`
// binding existed (compiler-internal package — nothing to preserve, unlike
// the PR #914 stdlib precedent), so the surface is fns only. Signature
// types (Stmt/Expr from ../core) are structural signature text resolved
// against the implementation import when the facade is merged in — same
// precedent as @vibe/symbol / @vibe/parser (no re-import needed here).

fn normalize_stmts(stmts: Array[Stmt]) -> Array[Stmt]
fn normalize_source(src: String) -> String with Error
fn lift_match_scrutinees(expr: Expr, counter: Array[Int]) -> Expr
fn uniquify_shadowed_bindings(expr: Expr, env: Map[String, String], counter: Array[Int], seen: Array[String]) -> Expr

// #1194 (ADR-0081): recv.method(args) -> Type::method(recv, args) where
// locally recoverable. Exported directly (in addition to being wired into
// normalize_stmts) so it's unit-testable on a bare Stmt list.
fn normalize_dot_calls(stmts: Array[Stmt]) -> Array[Stmt]
